</section>

<!-- MARQUEE -->
<div class="marquee"><div class="track">
  <div class="seg"><b>Walnut Blasting</b><b>Intake Valve Cleaning</b><b>Direct Injection</b><b>Restored Power</b><b>No Dealer Markup</b></div>
  <div class="seg"><b>Walnut Blasting</b><b>Intake Valve Cleaning</b><b>Direct Injection</b><b>Restored Power</b><b>No Dealer Markup</b></div>
</div></div>

<!-- STAT BAND -->
<section class="stats"><div class="container">
  <div class="statc"><b>Walnut</b><span>Blasting Media</span></div>
  <div class="statc"><b>BMW &amp; Audi</b><span>Direct Injection</span></div>
  <div class="statc"><b>OEM</b><span>Gaskets &amp; Seals</span></div>
  <div class="statc"><b>2010</b><span>Independent Since</span></div>
</div></section>

<!-- INTRO -->
<section class="sec">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Carbon cleaning, done right</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Why direct-injection BMWs choke on carbon.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose reveal">
      <p>Searching for <span class="kw">BMW carbon buildup cleaning</span> in San&nbsp;Antonio? Here's the why: modern BMW (and Audi) engines use direct injection, which sprays fuel straight into the cylinder instead of over the intake valves. That's great for power and efficiency — but it means the valves never get washed by fuel, so oil vapor from the crankcase bakes onto them as hard carbon over tens of thousands of miles. Eventually that crust chokes airflow and the engine runs rough.</p>
      <p>The only proper fix is mechanical: <span class="kw">walnut blasting</span>. We remove the intake manifold, seal off each port, and blast the valves with crushed walnut shell media — abrasive enough to strip carbon, soft enough to leave the valves unharmed. Chemical sprays and "fuel additives" can't touch baked-on intake-valve carbon; only media blasting truly cleans it. We reassemble with fresh OEM gaskets and verify the result.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SERVICES -->
<section class="sec alt">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">What's included</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Complete walnut-blasting service.</h2>
      <p class="lead">A thorough job — not a can of spray cleaner down the intake.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-grid">
      <div class="svc reveal"><div class="ico"><i data-lucide="search"></i></div><h3>Carbon Diagnosis</h3><p>We confirm carbon is the cause — borescope the valves and read fault codes — before any work.</p></div>
      <div class="svc reveal"><div class="ico"><i data-lucide="wind"></i></div><h3>Walnut Blasting</h3><p>Intake removed, ports sealed, valves media-blasted back to clean metal — the correct method.</p></div>
      <div class="svc reveal"><div class="ico"><i data-lucide="layers"></i></div><h3>Intake &amp; Gaskets</h3><p>Intake manifold cleaned and refitted with fresh OEM gaskets and seals on reassembly.</p></div>
      <div class="svc reveal"><div class="ico"><i data-lucide="git-commit-horizontal"></i></div><h3>Combine With Other Work</h3><p>Spark plugs, coils or a valve-cover gasket due? Doing it together saves labor since the top end is open.</p></div>
      <div class="svc reveal"><div class="ico"><i data-lucide="gauge"></i></div><h3>Before/After Check</h3><p>We verify smooth idle and clean running so you feel the restored power and economy.</p></div>
      <div class="svc reveal"><div class="ico"><i data-lucide="shield-check"></i></div><h3>Warrantied Work</h3><p>Backed by our 24-month / 24,000-mile guarantee, with OEM-quality parts throughout.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SYMPTOMS HOOK -->
<section class="sec">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="n54 reveal">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">BMW Carbon Symptoms</span>
        <h2>Does your BMW have carbon build-up?</h2>
        <p>Carbon comes on gradually, so owners often don't notice how much power they've lost until after a cleaning. If you drive a direct-injection N54, N55, N20, N63 or B58 BMW past roughly 60,000–80,000 miles, these are the tell-tale signs.</p>
        <p>Not sure? We'll borescope the valves and show you. For full BMW service, see our <a class="inline" href="/bmw-repair-san-antonio">BMW repair page</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="fail">
        <li><i data-lucide="activity"></i><span><b>Rough or shaky cold idle</b> and the occasional stall</span></li>
        <li><i data-lucide="alert-triangle"></i><span><b>Misfire codes</b> and hesitation under acceleration</span></li>
        <li><i data-lucide="gauge"></i><span><b>Lost power &amp; worse MPG</b> that crept in over time</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- BY MAKE -->
<section class="sec alt">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Direct-injection specialists</span>
      <h2 class="h2">BMW &amp; Audi carbon cleaning.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Both brands' direct-injection engines build carbon the same way — and we walnut-blast both.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="km-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;">
      <a class="kmcard reveal" href="/bmw-repair-san-antonio">
        <span class="kl"><img src="/assets/marques/bmw.svg" alt="BMW"></span>
        <h3>BMW</h3><p>N54, N55, N20, N63 &amp; B58 intake-valve walnut blasting.</p>
        <span class="kcta">BMW Service <i data-lucide="arrow-right"></i></span>
      </a>
